{"id": "wwdc2017-821", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/821", "wordCount": 1457, "segments": [{"start": 22.0, "text": "Hi everyone. Today we're going to talk about"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "something very colorful."}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "Display P3 and Wide Gamut, what"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "that is and how we use it."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "But first I want to mention"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "color management real quick."}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "With color management we make"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "sure that the display colors as"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "accurately as possible across"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "devices, platforms, and color"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "spaces."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "And color management is built"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "into both Mac OS and iOS."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "And color management helps avoid"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "a situation like this where"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "colors are incorrectly"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "represented going from source to"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "device."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "So as a designer makes sure to"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "tag your assets properly to"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "allow for color management to"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "accurately display your colors."}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "So what is then Display P3?"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "Very simply put it's a color"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "space within the RGB color model"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "that represents a larger"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "spectrum of colors than the"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "current industry standard sRGB."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "And most of us have been using"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "sRGB for probably over a decade"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "now, but with display P3 we get"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "a 25 percent larger color space"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "compared to sRGB."}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "This means that they can"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "represent more colors with"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "better accuracy and stay more"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "true to what those colors"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "actually look like in real life."}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "And in this image the black"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "strobe represents the size of"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "the sRGB color space and as you"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "can see the Display P3 extends"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "way beyond that."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "And when the color space is"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "larger than sRGB it is"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "informally referred to as a wide"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "gamut color space, also displays"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "supporting a larger color space"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "than sRGB referred to as wide"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "gamut displays."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "And the late 2015 iMac Retina"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "was the first consumer-facing"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "computer that supported Display"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "P3."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "When working with the Display P3"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "color profile you have the"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "opportunity to also use a larger"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "color depth."}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "16 bit per channel instead of"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "the usual 8."}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "That allows you to represent"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "more colors within the wide"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "gamut, which is especially"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "useful for gradients."}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "So let's take a look at an"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "example of that."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "Now this is a somewhat"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "exaggerated example, but clearly"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "we have banding happening in"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "this sRGB gradient."}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "Something i could try to get run"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "by using dithering."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "And it will look something like"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "Or if I instead use Display"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "P3and set my color depth to 16"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "bits per channel, then banding"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "is then much less visible."}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "We're simply closing the gap"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "between each defined color,"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "giving us a much better result."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "And we chose to display P3 for"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "its similarities to our existing"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "view and conditions that were"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "already defined in sRGB."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "Then by lining both the gamut"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "and the wide points, we get a"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "color space that behaves very"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "similar, making the threshold to"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "understand again working with"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "Display P3 much lower."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "But before we move on I want to"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "mention that since we're looking"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "at this presentation on sRGB"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "based projection system, all of"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "the examples in this"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "presentation are renditions,"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "which then leads me to who can"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "actually see Display P3 Images?"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "Well users needs a wide gamut"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "display that supports the"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "Display P3 color space and color"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "profile."}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "And Apple has supported wide"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "gamut displays since the late"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "2015 iMac Retina."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "But now there's a wider range of"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "devices that all support Display"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "P3 -- for example, the iPhone 7,"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "the MacBook Pro with a Touch Bar"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "and also the iPad Pro."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "But what about you as a"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "designer?"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "Because you do not want to be"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "flying blind when creating"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "Display P3 assets."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "You want full control over your"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "colors."}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "So make sure to work on a wide"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "gamut display that supports"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "Display P3 like the MacBook Pro"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "of the Touch Bar, the iMac"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "Retina, or the LG5K Display."}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "So now we know what display P3"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "is and how we can see it."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "Let's take a look at an example."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "In this beautiful image we have"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "some really nice colors."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "Some with wide ranges of red,"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "green, and orange."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "Now this is an sRGB image to"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "current standard."}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "But because of the limitations"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "within sRGB, not all colors that"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "were captured by the camera are"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "in this photo."}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "Represented here by these light"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "blue fields."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "Simply because these colors were"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "not available in the sRGB color"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "space."}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "The display P3 version of the"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "same image is a completely"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "different story."}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "Now we have rich, beautiful, and"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "bold colors throughout the"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "entire image."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "And if you compare the three"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "images we have a pretty"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "significant difference and I"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "almost feel a little bit sad for"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "out buddy here on the left."}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "He looks really bad right now."}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "OK, so let's take a look at the"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "Display P3 Workflow and we're"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "going to be using Photoshop."}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "And let's begin with a brand new"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "document, and in order to take"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "full advantage of all of the"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "colors available in the Display"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "P3 Color Space, the first thing"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "you need to do is to tag your"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "asset with the correct color"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "profile."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "So I'm creating that new"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "document in Photoshop, make sure"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "to set your color profile to"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "Display P3 like this."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "And the next thing I want to do"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "is to change the color depth"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "from 8 to 16 bits per channel"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "like this."}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "And once you're finished with"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "you're absolutely fantastic"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "design, it is now time to save"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "out your artwork."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "And there are multiple ways of"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "doing so on Photoshop like using"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "Generator or Export As."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "But in this case it is key then"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "to use Save As and PNG as your"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "format because this is the only"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "way at the moment to both imbed"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "a color profile and maintain the"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "color depth without -- in the"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "exported asset."}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "For example, Generator will not"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "imbed a color profile and leave"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "your asset entirely untagged."}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "So only use Save As."}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "When opening raw files in"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Photoshop, make sure to tag --"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "to change the color profile to"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "display P3 and the color depth"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "to 16 bits per channel by"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "clicking here."}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "Also, if you're receiving assets"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "from someone else, makes sure"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "that those assets are converted"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "to display P3 directly from the"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "raw file and not sRGB as the"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "color information would then"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "already be completely lost."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "So walk down your asset pipeline"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "and make sure you get Display P3"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "assets directly from your"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "source."}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "If you're working from an"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "existing asset like an app icon,"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "make sure to use Convert to"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "Profile."}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "This will actually perform a"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "color match operation and not"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "alter your design."}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "Click like that."}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "And do not use Assign to Profile"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "as that will take your existing"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "colors and stretch those out"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "into the new color space"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "changing your design in some"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "way."}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "So always use Convert to"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "profile."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "As an example let's look what"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "happens to the RGB of values"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "before and after converting to"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "display P3 from an sRGB"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "Gradient."}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "And we're going to look at the"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "red color spefically here."}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "Now in this sRGB image you can"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "see that I'll all the way up in"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "the top right corner and our RGB"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "values are then 255, 0, 0."}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "That's pretty much as red as it"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "gets."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "But after converting to display"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "P3 I can now see that I have a"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "lot more red to work with and I"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "can also see that my RGB values"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "has now changed."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "So you guys are now ready to go"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "and create stunning Display P3"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "Assets for your app."}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "But before you do take a second"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "and ask the question, should I?"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "Display P3 works great in some"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "cases, in others it's just not"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "the right choice."}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "For example, if your app is"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "designed with a calm,"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "de-saturated color scheme, it"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "doesn't use a lot of imagery,"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "display P3 might not be the"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "right choice for you."}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "But it is great for calling"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "attention to certain details"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "within your UI, such like a VU"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "meter or the red line in the rev"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "counter."}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "Or used to smooth out that app"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "icon gradient."}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "Or if your app uses a lot of"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "scenic imagery of nature,"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "landscapes, or travel"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "destinations, this use of"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "Display P3 makes a whole lot of"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "sense because these images will"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "look more vibrant and richer and"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "colors will stay more true to"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "what they actually looked like"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "when the camera captured that"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "very specific and special image."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "Or for apps that feature"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "textiles or garments were shown"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "the true color of a dress or a"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "pair of pants is immensely"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "important."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "So in conclusion, we have the"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "Display P3 color space and color"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "profile."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "It is 25 percent larger than"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "sRGB and lots of your users"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "already have compatible devices"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "in their hands today."}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "Then keep in mind the special"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "workflow when creating these"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "assets and make sure to use it"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "where it makes sense."}]}